BLOCKING 1 — zero recorded reds for eleven spec'd behaviours

  The brief lists eleven behaviours and closes that section with "Record the
  red for each before implementing." Engineering lex 2 makes it a clause a
  builder does not skip ("a behaviour is implemented only after its test has
  been run and shown failing, and that failure is kept as evidence") and lex
  7 makes it a condition of done ("the recorded red for every behaviour its
  spec listed").

  No red exists for any of the eleven. Searched: studio/ci/ (only the three
  gate logs per tree, plus the stale cascade-4b review note), the full
  history of studio/ci/* across all branches, and builder D's own worktree at
  .claude/worktrees/wf_f8104331-3d7-3, which is clean with nothing
  uncommitted. cascade-5/W-019 is a single squashed build commit; there is no
  red-then-green pair anywhere in it.

  ci/W-019-lint-0acb03d2.log is not behaviour 1's red. It records "npm run -s
  lint, exit code 1" because the script did not exist — that is the brief's
  Intent evidence. Behaviour 1's red is named precisely: "the pre-narrowing
  run's failing output", i.e. eslint under the deliberately broader rule set,
  shown failing, before the set was narrowed. That output was never captured,
  so the claim that the rule set was narrowed from a broader one rather than
  written narrow from the start has no evidence behind it. The same holds for
  behaviour 2, whose red is named just as precisely ("the same command with
  the four paths above un-ignored") and is equally absent.

  A red cannot be backfilled. Re-running these commands today, against a tree
  where the code already works, produces a green, not the red that was
  supposed to precede the code. This finding is therefore not remediable by
  producing evidence now, and it is fourth in a class the officina has failed
  on before: review x evidence-backfilled-or-absent, L-001, L-008, and W-016
  round 2 this same cascade.

  I record the same distinction the W-016 reviewer drew, because it is the
  honest one. The officina has no sanctioned place to store a per-behaviour
  red: ci/ holds gate logs keyed by source-tree hash and nothing else, and no
  CLI writes one. A builder told to keep a red has nowhere the model
  recognises to keep it. That mechanism gap is already escalated to the
  Patron on W-016 and W-019 cannot clear it from inside the opus either. It
  should be answered once, for both.

