ADVISORY 1 — .claude/worktrees/ is not gitignored, and it is silently
downgrading this cascade's certificates

  Not W-019's to fix — .gitignore is W-017's file and W-017 is halted — but
  it is this cascade's problem and it should not be lost.

  The cascade harness puts each builder's git worktree under
  .claude/worktrees/ inside the repo. Nothing ignores that path, so it shows
  as untracked and isDirtyOutside reports the tree dirty. It does not affect
  sourceTreeHash, which reads `git ls-tree` and so sees tracked files only.
  The result: the source tree is byte-identical to HEAD, and verify refuses
  to run anyway.

  That is where W-016's three dirty:9020672e certificates come from, and the
  three probatio.certifies.dirty advisories `check` now prints against it.
  They do not indicate that W-016 was verified against modified source. They
  indicate that the harness left its own scratch checkouts where git could
  see them. The honest reading of those three advisories is "harness
  artefact", not "W-016 certified a dirty tree", and whoever reviews W-016
  should know that before treating them as a defect.

  To run verify here I added .claude/worktrees/ to .git/info/exclude — local,
  uncommitted, outside the tree, and it changes no source file. That is a
  workaround for one session. The fix is one line in .gitignore, and it
  should be the first thing the opus that next owns that file does.

  Recommend: add .claude/worktrees/ to .gitignore alongside the existing
  local-state entries (receipts/, sessions/, timeline/, .bisellium/), which
  it belongs with for exactly the same reason — it is a machine's working
  state, not the studio's committed record.

ADVISORY 2 — eslint.config.mjs, not eslint.config.js

  The brief's Files-owned list says eslint.config.js; the opus shipped .mjs.
  Correct as built — the root package.json declares no "type": "module", so a
  flat config must be .mjs to load as ESM. Recorded so the next reader of the
